# Fluid 1: Pipe Networks

Water reaches a city through a network of pipes, and the first question about any network is steady: with these demands and these pipes, what are the pressures and flows? This chapter describes a network and checks it, solves a looped network and reads the solver's stopping rule, looks at the head-loss law each pipe obeys, and solves many scenarios at once while differentiating the answer.

- [Building a network](fluid_01_pipe_networks/building_a_network.md)
- [Looped networks](fluid_01_pipe_networks/looped_networks.md)
- [Pipe loss models](fluid_01_pipe_networks/pipe_loss_models.md)
- [Scenarios and sensitivities](fluid_01_pipe_networks/scenarios_and_sensitivities.md)

